Regional Market Insights
•	North America: Leads in product innovation and premium offerings, with the American Licorice Company's Red Vines brand dominating shelf space. The region shows strong preference for fruit-flavored variants over traditional black licorice.
•	Europe: Remains the bastion of traditional licorice consumption, particularly in Nordic countries and the Netherlands. The EU's strict glycyrrhizin regulations significantly influence product formulations across the region.
•	Asia-Pacific: Emerging as the fastest-growing market with Japan pioneering innovative textured varieties and Australia's Darrell Lea brand expanding regionally. Local flavor adaptations like yuzu and ginger are gaining traction.
•	Latin America: Shows growing interest in premium imported brands alongside developing domestic production capabilities in Brazil and Argentina.
•	Middle East & Africa: Experiencing steady growth driven by expatriate communities in Gulf countries, with halal-certified production becoming increasingly important.
